- action(n10, "Account Creation Rejected"): Hallucinates an intermediate action step; the source text directly connects the rejection outcome to termination ("In case of Account Creation Rejection, the process ends with the Account Creation being rejected"), making action(n8, "Account Creation is rejected") sufficient to precede end(e2) without an intervening node.
- actor(a_default, "Default", [...]): Misattributes process responsibilities; the source explicitly identifies the "User" as performing the initiation steps ("User Begin Creating Account", "User Create Account"), but the model assigns all nodes to a generic "Default" actor instead of mapping them to the stated participant.